<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-7">7 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Vietnamese forces capture Phnom Penh and topple the Khmer Rouge</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s army took the Cambodian capital, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pol-pot">Pol Pot</a>'s regime, under which some 1.5 to 2 million people had died. A decade of Vietnamese occupation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanoi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-17">17 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">China invades Vietnam</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Chinese troops crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s northern border to punish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a> for invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>. Both sides claimed victory after a month of fighting that cost tens of thousands of lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-26">26 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Israel sign a peace treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the White House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> and Menachem Begin signed the first peace treaty between Israel and an Arab state, building on the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords. Israel returned the Sinai by 1982.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-28">28 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Partial meltdown at Three Mile Island</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A cooling failure caused part of a reactor core to melt at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> nuclear plant. Little radiation escaped, but it was the worst US nuclear accident and stalled new reactor orders.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-4">4 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Thatcher becomes Britain's first woman Prime Minister</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Conservatives won the general election, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-thatcher">Margaret Thatcher</a> took office. In eleven years in power she privatised industries, curbed trade unions and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falklands-war">Falklands War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-18">18 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Carter and Brezhnev sign the SALT II treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The treaty capped each side's strategic nuclear launchers. The US Senate never ratified it after the Soviet invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, though both sides largely observed its limits.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-11">11 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Skylab falls to Earth over Western Australia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's Skylab space station broke up on re-entry, scattering debris near Esperance in Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>. The local shire jokingly fined NASA for littering; an American radio host paid the fine in 2009.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-19">19 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sandinista rebels take power in Nicaragua</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-debayle">Anastasio Somoza Debayle</a> fled, Sandinista forces entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/managua">Managua</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somoza-family">Somoza family</a>'s 43-year rule. The revolution soon drew the US into backing the Contra insurgency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-17">17 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mother Teresa is named winner of the Nobel Peace Prize</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Norwegian Nobel Committee announced its Peace Prize for Mother Teresa, founder of the Missionaries of Charity in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>, for her work among the poorest and dying.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-4">4 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Students seize the US embassy in Tehran</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Iranian students occupied the US embassy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> and took 66 hostages. Fifty-two were held for 444 days, a crisis that soured US-Iranian relations and damaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a>'s presidency.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kabul" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kabul.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-27">27 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet special forces kill Afghanistan's leader Hafizullah Amin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">As Soviet troops poured into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, commandos stormed the Tajbeg Palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and killed President Amin. The decade-long war that followed cost hundreds of thousands of Afghan lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sino-vietnamese-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-vietnamese-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sino-vietnamese-war">Sino-Vietnamese War</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sino-Vietnamese War was a brief war fought in February and March 1979, when China invaded northern Vietnam in response to Vietnam's invasion of Cambodia and its alliance with the Soviet Union.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-david">Hurricane David</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hurricane David was a Category 5 Atlantic hurricane that struck Dominica on 29 August 1979 and then the Dominican Republic and the south-eastern United States.</p></div></li></ol></section>
